hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1551","Bundar told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, and Yahya told us: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Talha al-Ayyami, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, he said: I heard Al-Baraa bin Aazib speaking, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to come to us when we stood for prayer and wipe Our shoulders and our chests, and He says: “Do not let your chests differ lest your hearts differ. Indeed, God and His angels pray in the first row,” and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Adorn the Qur’an.” Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja said: I had forgotten: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices,” until al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim reminded me."
"1552","Narrated by Issa bin Ibrahim, narrated by Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: I heard Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdhani, saying: Abdul Rahman narrated to me Ibn Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Baraa Ibn Aazib, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to come to us and wipe over our necks and chests. And he says: “Do not let your rows differ, lest your hearts differ. Indeed, God and His angels pray in the first row,” or “the first rows.”"
